WEBVTT

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.000
Meme...

00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:47.625
Meme, wake up.

00:00:47.625 --> 00:00:51.375
We're supposed to plant Halloween
pumpkins together today, remember?

00:00:53.208 --> 00:00:55.542
Imagine, pumpkins growing
from sprouts like this.

00:00:55.542 --> 00:00:57.667
I've never heard of such a thing.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:01.125
Look, Miss Anya is raring to go.

00:01:03.875 --> 00:01:06.042
Tsugumi, more, please.

00:01:06.042 --> 00:01:07.792
Huh?

00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:10.042
Whoa! Hold on!

00:01:10.042 --> 00:01:11.542
Meme!

00:01:11.542 --> 00:01:14.125
Oh, how soft...

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:23.292
<i>we wanna be there even if we had to</i>
<i>twist the world all around to get there</i>

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:34.167
<i>without you, i guess i couldn't</i>
<i>even find the future here today</i>

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:45.167
<i>i was always trying to take nothing for granted</i>

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:53.167
<i>for the day i might lose them</i>

00:01:53.167 --> 00:02:00.208
<i>but you just came in to my black</i>
<i>and white monochrome destiny</i>

00:02:00.208 --> 00:02:10.417
<i>and colored it all over</i>

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:17.750
<i>we won't be satisfied with the routine future</i>

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:25.208
<i>we were born to make a new history come true</i>

00:02:25.208 --> 00:02:32.375
<i>there's absolutely no</i>
<i>absolute thing in this world</i>

00:02:32.375 --> 00:02:36.958
<i>this road goes on forever</i>

00:02:36.958 --> 00:02:43.083
<i>as long as we won't give up</i>

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.000
"Pumpkin Growing!"

00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:58.125
They say that plants grow
better when you sing to them.

00:02:58.125 --> 00:02:59.833
Oh, is that right?

00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:01.792
Yes. Probably.

00:03:01.792 --> 00:03:04.167
More commoners' wisdom, huh?

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.750
"Sweltering Nights!"

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:15.708
Ugh, it's so hot...

00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:21.833
Whoa! Meme is walking around in her sleep again.

00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:24.167
Too hot...

00:03:25.833 --> 00:03:27.375
Why are you stripping down?!

00:03:27.375 --> 00:03:30.417
You can't do that, even if it is hot.

00:03:30.417 --> 00:03:32.625
If you sleep with your tummy
exposed, you'll catch a cold.

00:03:32.625 --> 00:03:35.500
Too hot...

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:39.000
Tsugumi, you've got something
tasty hidden away here, huh?

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.917
What are you talking about, Meme?

00:03:40.917 --> 00:03:45.042
No hoarding it all to yourself.
Give me some, too.

00:03:45.042 --> 00:03:50.042
W-Whoa, Meme! What are you doing?! Stop!

00:03:50.042 --> 00:03:54.208
As hot as it is now, you two
are clinging to each other again?!

00:03:58.042 --> 00:04:01.125
So this is Miss Meme's
fabled drunken boxing, is it?

00:04:01.125 --> 00:04:05.417
I know you're grouchy about it
being too hot to sleep, but calm down!

00:04:05.417 --> 00:04:07.750
She may look ridiculously slatternly,

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.792
but her guard is perfect.

00:04:09.792 --> 00:04:13.708
I've always wanted to try my hand
against Miss Meme's drunken boxing.

00:04:13.708 --> 00:04:17.458
Miss Anya, it's not right to do
this to Meme when she's half-asleep!

00:04:17.458 --> 00:04:20.208
Miss Tsugumi, this is a
good chance for you to determine

00:04:20.208 --> 00:04:22.833
which one of us is more fit
to be your partner, right?

00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:24.542
Aw, geez...

00:04:24.917 --> 00:04:28.958
Tsugumi... my good buddy...

00:04:28.958 --> 00:04:30.417
Here goes!

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.083
She threw me as though
she were tossing in her sleep.

00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:45.625
So these are the moves of a sleeping person?

00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:48.083
This is... drunken boxing!

00:04:54.708 --> 00:04:56.625
I'll stop you!

00:04:56.625 --> 00:04:57.500
Cramp!

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.417
A leg cramp?!

00:05:01.917 --> 00:05:05.208
Ah... That hurt...

00:05:05.208 --> 00:05:08.542
Her moves are too tricky;
there's no way to predict them.

00:05:08.542 --> 00:05:11.792
Stop! Stop! Stop!

00:05:11.792 --> 00:05:14.292
I know it's too hot to sleep,

00:05:14.292 --> 00:05:16.625
but this thrashing about is
keeping us even more awake.

00:05:16.625 --> 00:05:19.125
We've got an early start tomorrow,
so let's hurry and get to sleep!

00:05:19.125 --> 00:05:22.583
If we end things like this,
I'll have an even worse night of sleep.

00:05:22.583 --> 00:05:23.833
If you keep making this racket,

00:05:23.833 --> 00:05:27.458
there's no telling what
Miss Kim next door will say to us.

00:05:27.458 --> 00:05:29.458
Just close your eyes, and you'll fall asleep.

00:05:29.458 --> 00:05:31.958
I'll be collecting a nuisance fee for sure!

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.292
So hot...!

00:05:36.292 --> 00:05:37.792
So hot, so hot...!

00:05:37.792 --> 00:05:39.375
Hey!

00:05:41.958 --> 00:05:44.167
So hot!

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:46.833
H-H-Hey!

00:05:46.833 --> 00:05:48.250
Y-You're wide open!

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:49.583
You're wide open!

00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:54.833
You can't avoid my attack with
your shorts down around your knees!

00:05:54.833 --> 00:05:57.167
It's over!

00:05:57.167 --> 00:06:03.083
Ah... that's cool...

00:06:03.083 --> 00:06:05.167
Feels good...

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:07.833
How can you dare to behave like that?!

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:10.000
Miss Anya, why don't
you come sleep like this, too.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.875
She says it's cooler, and feels good.

00:06:13.875 --> 00:06:15.500
Come on.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.958
The warmth from you two is so... hot.

00:06:28.958 --> 00:06:31.917
♪ Scribbles in my notebook ♪

00:06:31.917 --> 00:06:34.708
♪ The breeze coming from the window ♪

00:06:34.708 --> 00:06:37.292
♪ Every time our gazes meet ♪

00:06:37.292 --> 00:06:40.500
♪ I give you a happy wink ♪

00:06:41.083 --> 00:06:45.125
"Oblivious!"

00:06:52.417 --> 00:06:55.958
How did I get like this?

00:06:55.958 --> 00:06:59.042
This is the girls' dorm kitchen, right?

00:07:01.542 --> 00:07:04.542
Money? And so much of it!

00:07:12.708 --> 00:07:15.708
What do I do?! I don't remember a thing!

00:07:17.583 --> 00:07:18.792
Are you okay?!

00:07:18.792 --> 00:07:20.417
Is something the matter?!

00:07:22.625 --> 00:07:24.458
What kind of getup is that?

00:07:24.458 --> 00:07:26.417
It's nothing at all.

00:07:26.417 --> 00:07:28.750
Oh! Meme, your eyebrows...

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.208
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:07:30.208 --> 00:07:32.042
You're missing one of them.

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:43.208
Meme!

00:07:45.583 --> 00:07:49.125
Huh? Eternal Feather, ma'am...

00:07:49.125 --> 00:07:50.250
Here!

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.083
Huh?

00:07:51.083 --> 00:07:53.583
Eh?! What is this?

00:07:53.583 --> 00:07:56.042
That's what I was going to ask.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.458
Sloth.

00:08:05.792 --> 00:08:10.625
What did I do yesterday
that made me wind up like this?

00:08:10.625 --> 00:08:13.917
I had Tsugumi draw on a new eyebrow...

00:08:16.083 --> 00:08:16.958
Yo!

00:08:16.958 --> 00:08:20.000
Ah, Kim, ma'am...

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.167
That's an odd hat.

00:08:22.958 --> 00:08:24.292
Miss Kim!

00:08:24.292 --> 00:08:28.042
Was I doing anything unusual yesterday?

00:08:28.042 --> 00:08:33.292
Unusual? I <i>did </i>see you
running down Grissom Street.

00:08:33.292 --> 00:08:35.000
Grissom Street?

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.042
You were wearing a jersey and
everything. Weren't you jogging?

00:08:38.042 --> 00:08:42.042
What, you don't remember,
even though you were doing it?

00:08:42.042 --> 00:08:43.958
Oh, come to think of it,

00:08:43.958 --> 00:08:47.833
there may have been a boy
saying something like "Wait up!"

00:08:49.125 --> 00:08:52.667
Thank you very much.

00:08:52.667 --> 00:08:54.833
Oh, one more thing!

00:08:54.833 --> 00:08:57.500
Your eyebrows were cuter the other way.

00:09:05.417 --> 00:09:09.333
Why would I have been running along here?

00:09:09.333 --> 00:09:13.167
Not to mention a boy, and all this money.

00:09:13.167 --> 00:09:17.833
Ah! Maybe I was running to deliver
the ransom for a kidnapped boy!

00:09:17.833 --> 00:09:21.167
Oh, the young lady from yesterday!

00:09:21.167 --> 00:09:24.208
Such a pretty face to be
doing something so crazy.

00:09:24.208 --> 00:09:27.375
Who knew you would actually do it!

00:09:27.375 --> 00:09:31.208
Do it? What are you talking about?

00:09:31.208 --> 00:09:32.917
You don't mean, yesterday...?

00:09:32.917 --> 00:09:35.542
I see you, young lady!

00:09:35.542 --> 00:09:40.000
How dare you take my precious--
Give it back to me!

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:40.333
Here.

00:09:40.333 --> 00:09:45.750
No, not that! It may be small,
but it's my reason for living!

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:49.000
Um, I don't remember anything.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.667
You don't remember?! Don't give me that!

00:09:51.667 --> 00:09:53.833
I'm sorry!

00:09:53.833 --> 00:09:55.875
Ah! Hold on, there!

00:10:03.583 --> 00:10:05.333
Watch out!

00:10:20.667 --> 00:10:22.750
A casino?

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:24.958
Why do you look like you're in need?

00:10:24.958 --> 00:10:27.250
This is Vegas.

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:36.750
Give us a break today.

00:10:55.625 --> 00:10:57.792
M-My head...

00:11:22.792 --> 00:11:26.208
Marianne?

00:11:26.208 --> 00:11:29.917
Thank goodness! I was so worried, Marianne!

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:40.333
That's right! I remember!

00:11:40.333 --> 00:11:44.500
Yesterday, I was jogging along Grissom Street...

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.583
Why don't you pull a street stall while you run?

00:11:46.583 --> 00:11:48.458
It will make for better training.

00:11:48.458 --> 00:11:52.292
Believing him, I pulled
the souvenir dealer's cart,

00:11:52.292 --> 00:11:54.500
and sprinted all-out!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.708
But I was going too fast,
and crashed at the turn!

00:12:00.333 --> 00:12:03.333
I was at a loss as to what to do, when...

00:12:03.333 --> 00:12:05.583
Why do you look like you're in need?

00:12:05.583 --> 00:12:07.667
This is Vegas.

00:12:10.208 --> 00:12:13.542
After I hit the jackpot,
won enough money for the repairs,

00:12:13.542 --> 00:12:16.083
and made the proprietor cry,

00:12:16.083 --> 00:12:19.083
I forgot what it was that I was doing.

00:12:19.083 --> 00:12:24.542
As for why I was out jogging
to begin with, the reason was...

00:12:24.542 --> 00:12:29.208
I ran into this young boy,
who was walking his sloth in the park.

00:12:31.417 --> 00:12:33.208
It was then that he said to me...

00:12:33.208 --> 00:12:35.833
Let me go!

00:12:35.833 --> 00:12:38.958
You fat lady!

00:12:38.958 --> 00:12:40.875
Not again!

00:12:42.125 --> 00:12:44.708
I'm fat?!

00:12:51.667 --> 00:12:54.583
Just you wait, young man!

00:12:54.583 --> 00:12:58.125
Ah! Marianne!

00:12:58.125 --> 00:13:00.375
After returning to the dorm from the casino,

00:13:00.375 --> 00:13:05.083
and leaving the sloth with
Miss Eternal Feather, who I passed by,

00:13:05.083 --> 00:13:08.417
I went to the bathroom
and got on the scale, when...

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:09.500
"Fat"

00:13:10.042 --> 00:13:11.750
I've gained weight!

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:14.292
Shocked by how heavy I was,

00:13:14.292 --> 00:13:16.667
and determined to set the dial back even a tick,

00:13:16.667 --> 00:13:19.125
I shaved off my eyebrow.

00:13:21.333 --> 00:13:25.208
I'd forgotten to take off all the souvenirs.

00:13:25.208 --> 00:13:28.583
I was able to pay for the
damages to the stall, though.

00:13:32.792 --> 00:13:34.958
I wonder if there are other times

00:13:34.958 --> 00:13:37.333
when I've forgotten things like this.

00:13:37.333 --> 00:13:43.250
Both troubled times and happy times.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:46.958
I don't want to forget my memories with you.

00:13:46.958 --> 00:13:48.792
I wonder if I will.

00:13:50.958 --> 00:13:56.375
Do you think Meme is all right?
She's been acting a little strange.

00:13:56.375 --> 00:13:56.917
"Bat Whistle"

00:13:56.917 --> 00:13:59.792
What's this?

00:13:59.792 --> 00:14:02.875
Death City's famous "bat whistle"?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.333
♪ Anywhere I see our dreams ♪

00:14:18.333 --> 00:14:21.208
♪ reflected in anything else ♪

00:14:21.208 --> 00:14:23.875
♪ the times pass by too quickly ♪

00:14:23.875 --> 00:14:26.583
♪ as though they were in a rush ♪

00:14:26.583 --> 00:14:30.000
"Three-man Baseball!"

00:14:30.667 --> 00:14:32.167
What could these be?

00:14:32.167 --> 00:14:35.375
A bat, a ball, and a glove?

00:14:35.375 --> 00:14:37.500
And a catcher's mitt, at that!

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:40.667
A glove? For holding stove pots?

00:14:40.667 --> 00:14:43.417
For the national pastime, baseball!

00:14:43.417 --> 00:14:45.958
"Baseball"?

00:14:45.958 --> 00:14:49.083
This is a great chance!
Would you like to try playing some baseball?

00:14:49.083 --> 00:14:52.375
Miss Tsugumi sure seems
worked up over this, huh?

00:14:52.375 --> 00:14:55.000
Long ago, I used to play baseball
with my brother and my dog, Pochi,

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.125
out at the vacant lot.

00:14:57.125 --> 00:15:01.333
Is this "baseball" a commoners' sport?

00:15:01.333 --> 00:15:04.375
It's a sport popular among commoners.

00:15:04.375 --> 00:15:08.167
That leaves me little choice.
All right, I'll accompany you.

00:15:08.167 --> 00:15:09.417
Hooray!

00:15:09.417 --> 00:15:11.917
All right, Miss Anya, would
you like to be our first batter?

00:15:11.917 --> 00:15:14.583
I'll start out as the pitcher!

00:15:14.583 --> 00:15:17.125
Okay, and I'll take flies!

00:15:17.125 --> 00:15:19.375
Oh, there she goes.

00:15:19.375 --> 00:15:24.125
A fly is a ball hit high in the
air by a batter, not a position.

00:15:24.125 --> 00:15:26.500
As far as the positions you cover,
they're "right" or "center"--

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:29.125
Never mind that, let's hurry and play!

00:15:29.125 --> 00:15:31.542
Oh, how gallant of you.

00:15:31.542 --> 00:15:35.125
The bat and the glove are
mutually exclusive, Lady Anya.

00:15:35.125 --> 00:15:37.250
You'll never hold both at the same time.

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:38.958
If those two ever got mixed together,

00:15:38.958 --> 00:15:41.542
baseball would fall apart!

00:15:41.542 --> 00:15:44.000
Aren't you getting a little crazy over baseball?

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.750
You're acting a little creepy, Miss Tsugumi.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:48.333
Ahem...

00:15:50.208 --> 00:15:53.500
Okay, I'll explain baseball in simple terms.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:59.333
I'll pitch the ball, and Miss Anya,
you'll hit it with the bat.

00:16:05.083 --> 00:16:06.250
Simple?

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:09.792
Eh? <i>That's </i>all baseball is? That's no fun.

00:16:09.792 --> 00:16:12.625
Wait, how can you say that?!

00:16:12.625 --> 00:16:14.625
Real baseball is played nine against nine,

00:16:14.625 --> 00:16:17.542
and the games are played in huge stadiums!

00:16:17.542 --> 00:16:21.958
Something as dull as this?
You don't need 18 people to do <i>this</i>.

00:16:21.958 --> 00:16:23.875
You've got it wrong!

00:16:23.875 --> 00:16:28.208
Okay, fine! If that's how you
want it, face one pitch from me!

00:16:28.208 --> 00:16:31.458
Allow me to show you
just how intense baseball is!

00:16:31.458 --> 00:16:33.833
In that case, please give me the bat.

00:16:33.833 --> 00:16:35.708
Oh, right.

00:16:40.875 --> 00:16:47.167
Oh, no! I was so caught up in
my challenge to show her baseball,

00:16:47.167 --> 00:16:49.875
but we're talking about Miss Anya, here.

00:16:49.875 --> 00:16:53.917
I never thought of myself as being
unathletic before coming to DWMA,

00:16:53.917 --> 00:16:57.125
but there's no way I can beat a meister.

00:16:57.125 --> 00:17:00.792
Then again, however
athletically gifted Miss Anya may be,

00:17:00.792 --> 00:17:06.125
she's never played baseball.
It's too soon to give up yet.

00:17:06.125 --> 00:17:10.333
Miss Tsugumi, what are you
waiting for? Hurry and throw the ball.

00:17:10.333 --> 00:17:12.833
Her batting form is a disaster, after all.

00:17:12.833 --> 00:17:15.333
And this ball...

00:17:15.333 --> 00:17:17.708
A light rubber ball like
this will be easy to spice up

00:17:17.708 --> 00:17:21.958
with some air resistance.
Miss Anya doesn't know baseball.

00:17:21.958 --> 00:17:27.333
She's never seen a fastball,
let alone a breaking ball.

00:17:27.333 --> 00:17:29.167
This could work!

00:17:29.167 --> 00:17:31.542
All right, here goes!

00:17:31.542 --> 00:17:34.167
Bring it on!

00:17:42.875 --> 00:17:45.042
I don't care, give me anything!

00:17:45.042 --> 00:17:47.542
Just break!

00:17:47.542 --> 00:17:52.542
It broke inside and hopped!
That makes it fairly hard to hit--

00:17:52.542 --> 00:17:56.750
Royal spear technique!

00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:59.167
A thrust?!

00:17:59.167 --> 00:18:02.542
What the--?!

00:18:02.542 --> 00:18:05.708
Nice batting!

00:18:05.708 --> 00:18:06.958
I knew it.

00:18:06.958 --> 00:18:10.917
Sure, Meme ended up knocking
it down with a super fine play,

00:18:10.917 --> 00:18:16.208
but I've been soundly defeated.
I'm sorry, Brother.

00:18:16.208 --> 00:18:19.917
I wasn't able to demonstrate
the intensity of baseball to her.

00:18:19.917 --> 00:18:21.667
Nice catch.

00:18:21.667 --> 00:18:23.875
It was an amazing hit.

00:18:23.875 --> 00:18:25.208
Miss Tsugumi,

00:18:25.208 --> 00:18:30.292
I've never seen a ball move
like that. It was very exciting.

00:18:30.292 --> 00:18:33.875
Baseball sure is fun.

00:18:33.875 --> 00:18:35.417
Really?

00:18:35.417 --> 00:18:38.208
Hey, girls!

00:18:38.208 --> 00:18:41.417
That glove, bat, and ball are mine!

00:18:41.417 --> 00:18:42.500
Huh?

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:46.042
Rental charges are $7 per hour, per person.

00:18:47.375 --> 00:18:49.500
Three outs...

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:55.292
♪ Suddenly, before you know it, ♪

00:18:55.292 --> 00:18:57.750
♪ they are tightening up ♪

00:18:57.750 --> 00:19:00.292
♪ as tight as a school uniform ♪

00:19:00.292 --> 00:19:03.458
♪ What do we have in our hands? ♪

00:19:03.458 --> 00:19:07.375
"From Death City with Love..."

00:19:09.125 --> 00:19:11.250
Are you writing a letter?

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:14.167
Yes. I'm sending it to my family back in Japan.

00:19:14.167 --> 00:19:16.333
Don't you two ever write?

00:19:19.458 --> 00:19:22.333
I plan to send them some items of interest,

00:19:22.333 --> 00:19:25.292
and have them learn more about their uniqueness.

00:19:25.292 --> 00:19:28.917
Oh, yeah? What about you, Meme?

00:19:28.917 --> 00:19:31.625
I'm having a little trouble remembering.

00:19:31.625 --> 00:19:33.708
Is she evading the question?

00:19:41.375 --> 00:19:44.208
Hmm? It's the middle of the night...

00:19:51.375 --> 00:19:55.417
Are those cousins to the
messenger pigeons, messenger bats?!

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:00.500
No developments in the
witch Shaula investigation, then?

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:04.583
She's been keeping herself scarce
since the Eternal Feather incident.

00:20:04.583 --> 00:20:08.375
If she's a control-type witch,
I doubt she can be too far away,

00:20:08.375 --> 00:20:11.583
but we still don't have
any leads as to where she is.

00:20:13.167 --> 00:20:16.417
This may have nothing to do with witches, but...

00:20:19.833 --> 00:20:24.000
Lately, there has been a
rash of robberies within DWMA.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:26.958
This is a list of the stolen items.

00:20:26.958 --> 00:20:30.917
The restricted browsing collections
and past investigation records.

00:20:30.917 --> 00:20:34.333
They're after information
of a fairly high secret level.

00:20:35.792 --> 00:20:38.875
A list of meisters and weapons?

00:20:38.875 --> 00:20:42.792
We haven't been able to
make any links to Shaula yet.

00:20:42.792 --> 00:20:46.375
If we're lucky, this could be the
breakthrough in our investigation.

00:20:46.375 --> 00:20:48.083
Keep running down this thread.

00:20:48.083 --> 00:20:49.417
Right.

00:20:49.417 --> 00:20:52.750
That's all for today.
Thanks for staying so late.

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:55.917
Not at all. It's our duty.

00:20:55.917 --> 00:20:59.375
You won't be able to enter
this year's Battle Festival, either.

00:20:59.375 --> 00:21:02.792
The Battle Festival is a
tournament for the EAT class.

00:21:02.792 --> 00:21:06.000
And since we're now in the NOT class...

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:09.167
Maybe we can dress up,
and get some candy, instead.

00:21:09.167 --> 00:21:09.875
Huh?

00:21:09.875 --> 00:21:12.375
The Battle Festival is
held on Halloween, after all.

00:21:12.375 --> 00:21:14.625
We could dress up as
witches to hunt for witches.

00:21:14.625 --> 00:21:15.750
Are you serious?

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:20.667
It's your job to be skeptical,
but you sure do buy things easily, Clay.

00:21:20.667 --> 00:21:22.792
Oh, shut up!

00:21:22.792 --> 00:21:25.417
♪ Ah, here you are, next to me ♪

00:21:25.417 --> 00:21:29.542
♪ I've been waiting for this miracle ♪

00:21:29.542 --> 00:21:33.292
♪ for so long ♪

00:21:36.167 --> 00:21:39.208
♪ Scribbles in my notebook ♪

00:21:39.208 --> 00:21:41.958
♪ The breeze coming from the window ♪

00:21:41.958 --> 00:21:44.500
♪ Every time our gazes meet ♪

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:47.750
♪ I give you a happy wink ♪

00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:50.542
♪ Anywhere I see our dreams ♪

00:21:50.542 --> 00:21:53.500
♪ reflected in anything else ♪

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:56.167
♪ the times pass by too quickly ♪

00:21:56.167 --> 00:21:58.833
♪ as though they were in a rush ♪

00:21:58.833 --> 00:22:02.375
♪ Suddenly, before you know it, ♪

00:22:02.375 --> 00:22:04.833
♪ they are tightening up ♪

00:22:04.833 --> 00:22:07.417
♪ as tight as a school uniform ♪

00:22:07.417 --> 00:22:11.667
♪ What do we have in our hands? ♪

00:22:11.667 --> 00:22:14.417
♪ Ah, you've always been competing ♪

00:22:14.417 --> 00:22:17.333
--So on the day of the Battle Festival,
--♪ here at my side ♪

00:22:17.333 --> 00:22:18.958
--it's either Miss Meme, or me.
--♪ It's because you're here with me ♪

00:22:18.958 --> 00:22:20.417
--Please choose one or the other
--♪ It's because you're here with me ♪

00:22:20.417 --> 00:22:23.458
--for your partner on that day.
--♪ that I was able to come this far ♪

00:22:23.458 --> 00:22:25.792
♪ Though it's my first time here ♪

00:22:25.792 --> 00:22:28.792
♪ I'm not afraid ♪

00:22:28.792 --> 00:22:32.042
♪ As long as you're here, ♪

00:22:32.042 --> 00:22:34.750
♪ it becomes as familiar as home ♪

00:22:43.875 --> 00:22:46.292
Trick or Treat.

00:22:47.542 --> 00:22:51.708
<i>With a big wave and a "See you,"</i>

00:22:51.708 --> 00:22:58.625
<i>let's meet in the new day</i>

00:23:15.375 --> 00:23:19.542
<i>Our shadows stretch along the pavement</i>

00:23:19.542 --> 00:23:23.542
<i>coming together, then apart, then together</i>

00:23:23.542 --> 00:23:31.875
<i>What do I say when the road home ends?</i>

00:23:31.875 --> 00:23:36.042
<i>You are not alone. Nope, right nearby,</i>

00:23:36.042 --> 00:23:40.167
<i>there are eyes looking back at you</i>

00:23:40.167 --> 00:23:44.292
<i>And just like a miracle,</i>

00:23:44.292 --> 00:23:48.042
<i>they can turn even failures into laughter</i>

00:23:48.042 --> 00:23:52.167
<i>Thank you for a fun day</i>

00:23:52.167 --> 00:23:56.500
<i>Let's do it again tomorrow</i>

00:23:56.500 --> 00:24:00.583
<i>We'll open a brand-new door</i>

00:24:00.583 --> 00:24:04.750
<i>chasing after dreams and love</i>

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:10.375
<i>and those nameless feelings, too</i>

00:24:18.292 --> 00:24:21.583
I'm sorry I hurt you, Tsugumi.

00:24:21.583 --> 00:24:24.250
Meme? Meme, where are you going?!

00:24:24.250 --> 00:24:26.250
I can't believe we're parting like this.

00:24:26.250 --> 00:24:29.708
Miss Anya? What's going on? You, too, Miss Anya?

00:24:29.708 --> 00:24:32.192
"Next time: The Beginning of the Nightmare!"
This isn't a dream, is it?
